WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:07.381
The nightly settlement DAG has three tasks: extract, load and report.

2
00:00:07.381 --> 00:00:13.487
Each starts when the one before it finishes, and each run is for one day, here 6 November.

3
00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:19.872
At minute 5, extract copies the day's 235 payments into a staging partition.

4
00:00:20.067 --> 00:00:21.736
Take two versions of load.

5
00:00:21.736 --> 00:00:23.982
One appends a row with INSERT INTO.

6
00:00:23.982 --> 00:00:26.871
The other replaces the day's whole partition.

7
00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:34.688
At minute 15, attempt 1 writes the day's total, 5,974,657 cents.

8
00:00:34.688 --> 00:00:37.652
So far both tables agree.

9
00:00:37.867 --> 00:00:40.708
Then the worker dies before it reports success.

10
00:00:40.708 --> 00:00:47.117
The write is committed, but the orchestrator never heard back, so it marks the attempt failed and retries.

11
00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:49.299
Attempt 2 does the same work.

12
00:00:49.299 --> 00:00:51.849
The appending table now has two rows.

13
00:00:51.849 --> 00:00:54.744
The other table just replaces its one row.

14
00:00:54.933 --> 00:00:56.997
Report sums the day.

15
00:00:56.997 --> 00:01:05.976
The appending table says 11,949,314 cents, twice the truth, and every task shows green.

16
00:01:06.167 --> 00:01:12.829
The other table says 5,974,657, which is right.

17
00:01:13.033 --> 00:01:16.052
A week later, a backfill reruns 6 November.

18
00:01:16.052 --> 00:01:18.088
The append gains a third row.

19
00:01:18.088 --> 00:01:20.264
The other table doesn't change.

20
00:01:20.433 --> 00:01:25.859
That task is idempotent: running it twice leaves the same result as running it once.

21
00:01:26.067 --> 00:01:27.606
Two rules get you there.

22
00:01:27.606 --> 00:01:31.519
Read a fixed input, the run's own day, never the latest data.

23
00:01:31.519 --> 00:01:35.047
And write by replacing that day, never by adding to it.

24
00:01:35.233 --> 00:01:38.448
Retries and backfills both just run a task again.

25
00:01:38.448 --> 00:01:42.713
Make each task replace its own day, and running it again is safe.
